## Bilinear PatchMesh, nonperiodic on both axes: nu=3 nv=2, two patches
## side by side sharing their middle column of control points -- the
## smallest grid that exercises sub-patch selection rather than
## degenerating to a single "Patch bilinear". Same flat, unlit shading as
## patch_norender.rib: interpolation of a flat grid has no shading detail
## worth pixel-regression protection.
##
## A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
## desync convention."
Display "patchmesh_bilinear.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Sides 2
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
AttributeBegin
	Translate -1 0 0
	PatchMesh "bilinear" 3 "nonperiodic" 2 "nonperiodic" "P" [
		-0.5 -0.3 0   0 -0.3 0   0.5 -0.3 0
		-0.5  0.3 0   0  0.3 0   0.5  0.3 0
	]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
	Translate 1 0 0
	Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
